            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The hospitalisation of a child involves the whole family. The parents' perception is therefore a suitable indicator to help improve family-centered helpgiving practices. A study was carried out in 2014 in a paediatric unit in Switzerland, in order to guide the cultural adaptation of a tool for measuring the practices in place to support the parents of hospitalised children. The purpose is also that they know better their abilities.</AbstractText>
